Fall back to the meson on PATH when the build venv has none

OpenEmbedded's python3-native patches Lib/sysconfig.py so that 'base' and
'platbase' always come from the build configuration prefix rather than
sys.prefix (see poky's
meta/recipes-devtools/python/python3/0001-Lib-sysconfig.py-use-prefix-value-from-build-configu.patch).
As a result sysconfig.get_path('purelib'/'scripts') inside QEMU's pyvenv
resolves to recipe-sysroot-native rather than to the venv, so:

  - mkvenv considers the sysroot's meson-native to live "inside" the venv,
    so _is_system_package() returns False and it reinstalls meson,
  - pip and generate_console_scripts() then write the package and the
    'meson' console script into recipe-sysroot-native/usr/{lib,bin},

and pyvenv/bin/meson is never created, making configure fail with
"meson setup failed" / "pyvenv/bin/meson: not found".

Meson is perfectly usable from the recipe sysroot, so fall back to the one
on PATH when the venv did not get its own copy. Poky works around the same
issue in meta/recipes-devtools/qemu/qemu/fixedmeson.patch.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [workaround, needs a real fix in oe-core's python3-native]

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -986,6 +986,16 @@
   meson="$meson$EXESUF"
 fi

+# OpenEmbedded/Yocto: python3-native reports the *sysroot* paths from
+# sysconfig even when running inside a virtual environment (see
+# meta/recipes-devtools/python/python3/0001-Lib-sysconfig.py-use-prefix-value-from-build-configu.patch),
+# so pip and mkvenv install packages and console scripts into the recipe
+# sysroot instead of pyvenv/. Meson is perfectly usable from there, so fall
+# back to the one on PATH when the venv did not get its own copy.
+if ! test -e "$meson" && has meson; then
+    meson=$(command -v meson)
+fi
+
 # On Haiku, meson might show up in a "non-packaged" subfolder instead, see
 # https://github.com/haiku/haiku/blob/r1beta5/docs/user/storage/storageintro.dox
 if test "$host_os" = "haiku" && test ! -e "$meson" ; then
